WEBVTT

1
00:00:09,467 --> 00:00:11,261
[SOFT PIANO MUSIC PLAYING]

2
00:00:52,135 --> 00:00:54,387
[THUNDER RUMBLING]

3
00:00:54,471 --> 00:00:57,932
MAN:
♪ I telegraphed and phoned ♪

4
00:00:58,016 --> 00:01:02,604
♪ I sent air mail
special, too ♪

5
00:01:03,229 --> 00:01:05,065
Yeah, I know.

6
00:01:05,148 --> 00:01:11,071
♪ Answer was goodbye
There was even postage due ♪

7
00:01:13,782 --> 00:01:15,075
[THUNDER RUMBLING]

8
00:01:15,158 --> 00:01:19,204
♪ I fell in love just once ♪

9
00:01:19,287 --> 00:01:21,748
♪ And then it had
to be with you ♪

10
00:01:22,624 --> 00:01:23,875
Triple rhyme.

11
00:01:26,419 --> 00:01:32,092
♪ Everything happens to me ♪

12
00:01:37,055 --> 00:01:38,431
Oh, fuck.

13
00:01:39,724 --> 00:01:40,850
[GROANS]

14
00:01:42,227 --> 00:01:43,645
Yeah.

15
00:01:43,728 --> 00:01:45,396
ANNOUNCER: [ON RADIO]
WQXR notes the passing

16
00:01:45,480 --> 00:01:47,982
of one of America's
foremost songwriters,

17
00:01:48,066 --> 00:01:50,360
Lorenz Hart,
who died last night

18
00:01:50,443 --> 00:01:52,278
at Doctors Hospital
in Manhattan

19
00:01:52,362 --> 00:01:54,364
from complications
of pneumonia.

20
00:01:54,447 --> 00:01:57,408
Mr. Hart was 48 years old.

21
00:01:57,492 --> 00:02:01,204
For over 20 years, Hart and
his partner, Richard Rodgers,

22
00:02:01,287 --> 00:02:03,915
Rodgers wrote the music,
Hart the words,

23
00:02:03,998 --> 00:02:06,167
combined their
respective geniuses

24
00:02:06,251 --> 00:02:09,170
to create a string
of musical-comedy hits.

25
00:02:09,254 --> 00:02:12,549
Often referred to as America's
Gilbert and Sullivan,

26
00:02:12,632 --> 00:02:15,635
Rodgers and Hart will be
remembered for such songs as,

27
00:02:15,718 --> 00:02:18,596
My Funny Valentine,
The Lady Is A Tramp,

28
00:02:18,680 --> 00:02:20,056
Where or When,

29
00:02:20,140 --> 00:02:22,976
With A Song In My Heart,
Isn't It Romantic?,

30
00:02:23,059 --> 00:02:25,395
My Heart Stood Still, Bewitched,

31
00:02:25,478 --> 00:02:28,481
I Didn't Know What Time It Was,
Manhattan,

32
00:02:28,565 --> 00:02:29,816
and Blue Moon.

33
00:02:30,775 --> 00:02:32,610
[CHOIR VOCALIZING]

34
00:02:34,070 --> 00:02:36,364
♪ Okla-Okla-Okla-Okla-Okla ♪

35
00:02:36,447 --> 00:02:38,867
♪ Okla-Okla-Okla-Okla-Okla ♪

36
00:02:38,950 --> 00:02:41,828
♪ We know we belong
to the land ♪

37
00:02:41,911 --> 00:02:43,580
Here comes "grand."

38
00:02:43,663 --> 00:02:45,123
♪ And the land we belong to
is grand ♪

39
00:02:45,206 --> 00:02:47,417
♪ And when we say ♪

40
00:02:47,500 --> 00:02:51,212
♪ Yow! Ayipioeeay! ♪

41
00:02:51,296 --> 00:02:52,839
♪ We're only sayin' ♪

42
