52
00:03:28,875 --> 00:03:30,084
[DOOR OPENS]

53
00:03:50,980 --> 00:03:55,526
All right. For the last time,
put the letters on the table.

54
00:03:55,610 --> 00:03:58,488
"If Laszlo and the cause
mean that much to you,

55
00:03:58,571 --> 00:04:01,199
"you won't stop at anything."

56
00:04:01,282 --> 00:04:04,911
All right,
I'll make it easy on you.

57
00:04:04,994 --> 00:04:08,331
"Go ahead, shoot.
You'd be doing me a favor."

58
00:04:08,414 --> 00:04:11,042
Just remember, I got this gun
pointed at your dick.

59
00:04:11,125 --> 00:04:13,419
Oh. That's my least
vulnerable spot.

60
00:04:13,503 --> 00:04:15,129
[BOTH LAUGHING]

61
00:04:15,213 --> 00:04:16,547
BARTENDER: Jesus Christ!

62
00:04:16,631 --> 00:04:17,882
How many times
have we seen that picture?

63
00:04:17,966 --> 00:04:20,260
Worst line in Casablanca?

64
00:04:20,343 --> 00:04:24,097
"Well, a precedent
is being broken."

65
00:04:24,180 --> 00:04:25,974
"A precedent is being broken"?

66
00:04:26,057 --> 00:04:28,726
How can you break
a goddamn precedent?

67
00:04:28,810 --> 00:04:32,563
Do they even speak English
over there in Hollywood?

68
00:04:32,647 --> 00:04:35,149
Still, you have
to love Claude Rains.

69
00:04:35,233 --> 00:04:38,528
-He makes that picture.
-Sure.

70
00:04:38,611 --> 00:04:39,862
HART: You know
why he's so great?

71
00:04:39,946 --> 00:04:42,573
He's a leading man,
and he's short,

72
00:04:42,657 --> 00:04:45,076
which proves you can be both.

73
00:04:45,159 --> 00:04:46,452
And I love this.

74
00:04:46,536 --> 00:04:48,413
He says to Ilsa,

75
00:04:48,496 --> 00:04:53,293
"Mademoiselle, he's the kind
of man that, if I were a woman

76
00:04:53,376 --> 00:04:56,212
"and I were not around,
I should be in love with Rick."

77
00:04:56,296 --> 00:04:58,214
-[CHUCKLES]
-Think about it.

78
00:04:58,298 --> 00:05:00,800
Whom does he end up with
at the end of the picture?

79
00:05:00,883 --> 00:05:04,554
Who's strolling away together
arm in arm into the fog?

80
00:05:04,637 --> 00:05:06,264
You're saying Rick
and Captain Renault...

81
00:05:06,347 --> 00:05:07,682
What do you think goes on
over there

82
00:05:07,765 --> 00:05:10,018
at the Free French garrison
in Brazzaville?

83
00:05:10,101 --> 00:05:12,687
That is a scene
they can't show you.

84
00:05:12,770 --> 00:05:15,273
Okay. Best line in Casablanca?

85
00:05:17,817 --> 00:05:19,986
HART AND BARTENDER: "Nobody ever
loved me that much."

86
00:05:20,069 --> 00:05:21,738
Isn't that magnificent?

87
00:05:21,821 --> 00:05:25,074
Six words. "Nobody ever loved me
that much."

88
00:05:25,158 --> 00:05:27,243
[SCOFFS] And, really,
who's ever been loved enough?

89
00:05:27,327 --> 00:05:28,661
Who's ever been loved
half enough?

90
00:05:28,745 --> 00:05:29,704
Would you get me a shot?

91
00:05:31,247 --> 00:05:32,206
Larry, you told me
under no circumstances...

92
00:05:32,290 --> 00:05:33,541
I'm just going to look at it.

93
00:05:33,624 --> 00:05:34,584
-[INHALES DEEPLY]
-Take the measure

94
00:05:34,667 --> 00:05:36,961
of its amber heft in my hand.

95
00:05:37,045 --> 00:05:39,464
-You told me not...
-Just give me the drink.

96
00:05:39,547 --> 00:05:41,007
[EXHALES DEEPLY]

97
00:05:45,011 --> 00:05:46,721
Did I tell you
what Elizabeth told me?

98
00:05:46,804 --> 00:05:48,639
That's the girl
I'm meeting here tonight.

99
00:05:48,723 --> 00:05:50,475
-You mean the one you...
-Eddie, Eddie, Eddie.

100
00:05:50,558 --> 00:05:53,936
-What?
-Show some class, all right?

101
00:05:54,020 --> 00:05:56,147
Her mother is going to come
walking in here any second.

102
00:05:56,230 --> 00:05:57,982
-Sorry.
-Seriously.

103
00:05:58,066 --> 00:06:00,485
I... I adore this girl.

104
00:06:00,568 --> 00:06:02,612
And, I'm telling you,
this is beyond sex.

105
00:06:02,695 --> 00:06:04,864
-What's beyond sex?
-I don't understand it.

106
00:06:04,947 --> 00:06:06,824
She's completely undeserving,

107
00:06:06,908 --> 00:06:09,035
but isn't that the way
it always is?

108
00:06:09,118 --> 00:06:10,578
"Irrational adoration."

109
00:06:10,661 --> 00:06:11,996
That's the phrase
she came up with.

110
00:06:12,080 --> 00:06:13,873
She's a poet, too.
Did I tell you that?

111
00:06:13,956 --> 00:06:16,459
Oh, and would you give me
a shot of club soda?

112
00:06:16,542 --> 00:06:20,254
I'll drink one
and admire the other.

113
00:06:20,922 --> 00:06:22,423
So, this girl...

114
00:06:24,425 --> 00:06:27,720
You really, you know,

115
00:06:27,804 --> 00:06:30,139
